-- title:
--   Re-gluing a bare deformation by a tangent 1-cocycle
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an Artinian local ring $B$ with algebraically closed residue field, and a $B$-algebra $B_1$ whose structure map is surjective with nilpotent kernel $J=\ker(B\to B_1)$ satisfying $J\cdot\mathfrak m_B=0$ and $J\subseteq\mathfrak m_B$, with $q$ nilpotent in $B$. Assume given $f_1:A_1\to\operatorname{Spec}B_1$ with a commutative relative group law $L_1$ and the bundle of properties (smooth, proper, connected fibres, group law) of an abelian scheme; a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $B$ together with formal coordinates $\theta_1$ for $L_1$ adapted to the base change of $F$ to $B_1$; the hypothesis that every $q^m$-torsion point of $L_1$ over a $B_1$-algebra $C$ is infinitesimal along some nilpotent ideal of $C$; and the height condition that for each surjection $\rho:B\to k$ onto a field the quotient of $k[[x_1,x_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the $q$-th iterate series of $F.\mathrm{map}\,\rho$ has $k$-dimension $q^4$. Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional module over the residue field of $B$, equipped with compatible $B$- and opposite actions, and $\iota:V\to B$ an injective $B$-linear map whose image is $J$. Let $D_0$ be a bare deformation of $(f_1,L_1)$ to $B$ with separated structure map, $\mathcal U$ a finite ordered affine open cover of $D_0.A$, $i_0$ an index, and $e_0$, $e_1$ factorisations of the unit section of $D_0.L$, respectively of its base change to the residue field, through the chart $U_{i_0}$, respectively through the corresponding chart of the base-changed cover. Let $\sigma_s$, for each overlap index $s\in\mathcal U.\mathrm{Idx}\,1$, be ring isomorphisms $\mathrm{ResidueField}(B)\otimes_B\Gamma(D_0.A,\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s)\cong\Gamma$ of the corresponding overlap on the special fibre, compatible with the two canonical maps. Finally let $c$ be a point derivation, at the unit point $e_1$, of the ring of the special-fibre chart at $i_0$, with values in the space of linear maps from the dual of $V$ to the Čech $1$-cochains of the structure presheaf for the base-changed cover, such that every value $c(a)(\xi)$ lies in the kernel of the Čech differential $d^1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of self-isomorphisms $\tau_s$ of each overlap $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s$ and of a bare deformation $D$ of $(f_1,L_1)$ to $B$ such that $D_0$ is re-glued by $\mathcal U$ and $\tau$ into $D$ (the $\tau_s$ are maps over $\operatorname{Spec}B$ fixing the restrictions of $D_0.g$, and $D$ carries open immersions of the charts $\mathcal U.U\,i$ covering it, over $D_0.f$, compatible with $D_0.g$, whose transition on each overlap is twisted by $\tau_s$), and such that for each $s$ there is a map $c_s$ from the ring of the special-fibre chart at $i_0$ to the linear maps from the dual of $V$ to $\mathrm{ResidueField}(B)\otimes_B\Gamma(D_0.A,\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s)$ which is a system of tangent coordinates, in the sense of `IsTangentCoordsOfPairAt` for the ideal $J$, $V$ and $\iota$, for the pair consisting of the canonical map from the spectrum of $\Gamma(D_0.A,\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s)$ to $D_0.A$ and of the same map composed with $\tau_s$ and the open inclusion, relative to the base-changed group law and chart at $i_0$; and $\sigma_s\circ c_s$ agrees with the $s$-component of $c$.
--
--   This is the re-gluing step of the deformation theory of abelian schemes along a small extension $B\to B_1$: a Čech $1$-cocycle of $V$-valued tangent fields on the special fibre, expressed in the canonical tangent coordinates at the unit section, is realised by twisting the charts of a given bare deformation, producing a new bare deformation whose overlap comparisons have prescribed tangent coordinates. It is used in the construction of formal coordinates for lifted deformations and in the analysis of the point-derivation action on the set of bare deformations.
